            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy: how I do it.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e14-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SLE.0b013e318274b8cf</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG) is considered a straightforward procedure but the surgical technique is one of the major determinants of the success of this procedure. We describe a 3-port approach to LSG that was adopted in 750 consecutive cases. The LSG was completed with 4 cartridges in 712 cases (95%) and was associated with a 4.8% rate of complications including a 2.4% rate of leak. The surgical technique is described in detail and the inherent advantages are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
